# Copilot: a shell rule needs `:*` to match the command with any arguments; Copilot ignores a bare
# three-word `shell(gh pr comment)`. `write` is denied whole: a read-only or planning Copilot writes its report or
# plan under `$(mesh dir)` with the shell (or sends it with `--body`).
COPILOT_DENY = ("write", *(f"shell({cmd}:*)" for cmd in PUBLISH_COMMANDS))
# Copilot's rate-limit messages (`copilot help limits`): "You've hit the rate limit for this model.", "You've hit
